      "content": "Frame the argument by using the concept of aggregate demand outpacing aggregate supply, which is a rigorous economic principle. Propose that injecting a massive, non-productive stream of guaranteed cash (UBI) into an economy with fixed or slow-growing production capacity will mathematically guarantee that demand surges beyond available goods. This demand chasing scarcity acts as a direct accelerator of price levels, leading to runaway inflation that quickly erodes UBI's real value, rendering the entire program meaningless.",
